# Hedon: Bloodrite

## MAP01: Cold Rock

Power cores aren't permanently deducted from your inventory when used (AP treats
them as keys and returns them to your inventory). Instead, you won't be able to
repair the elevator until you've found two power cores, and will need to have
found three to repair the gate.

The northwest caves, normally reached via the iron key, can also be reached by
opening the timed gate in the outpost and exiting to the pond room. The gate
will close behind you but you can get back into the outpost by swimming through
an underwater tunnel on the west side of the pond.

The wooded area unlocked by offering a moonflower is not considered a secret
for the purposes of logic, but the hidden baths to the east are.

## MAP02: Plaza

There are several ways to get into the park, all of them in logic:
- use the iron key to flip the park switch in the south guardhouse, as in vanilla;
- use the vine key to enter the alchemist's shop and jump off the balcony;
- use the axe key to enter the north smithy, fall into the well, and follow the
  caves and river clockwise until you enter the library via the ventilation shaft.

The arena fight in the west plaza (that opens an alternate path to the north
plaza when finished) is triggered by entering the west plaza while carrying the
stone key. This means that just having the key is logically sufficient to access
the north plaza.

The arena fight also closes the park gate and the gate connecting the east and
west plazas. You can get back to the east plaza by going north and climbing into
the inn through the window (or using the axe key to open the back door, if you
have it). You can get back to the garden using any of the techniques above, but
note that the guardhouse switch is not repeatable; if that's your only way into
the garden and you missed any items there, you'll need to reset the level so
that you can use the switch again.

## MAP03: Barracks

A very straightforward map. Note that while the Stone Key unlocks a shortcut
between the sparring room and the firing range, the only thing it's actually
needed for is accessing the north power control room.

## MAP04: Technical Space

Restoring the power is optional if you have the toolkit, although some checks
in the starting areas depend on it.

Reaver Tiati's departure is triggered by exiting the Great Forge in the
direction of the portal room while carrying the Iron Key (and this is necessary
to check the items she leaves behind). In AP it is possible to bypass this
trigger by toggling the key off, which lets you access the portal room with the
portal still online. However, entering the portal gets you a game over (and
there are no checks behind it); save first if you want to try this.

The iron and mithril ores you can mine out of the walls are checks, and require
the pickaxe.

The fabrication machines in and around the Great Forge also produce checks the
first time you use them; subsequent uses will produce either unusable key
duplicates (in the case of key item fabricators) or their normal vanilla items
(in the case of ammo/item fabricators). Since all of their inputs are key items
and keys are infinitely re-usable in AP, you don't need to worry about picking
and choosing which machines to activate.

The following machines are available:

- Iron Ore -> Iron Ingot in Dwarven Forge
- Iron Ingot -> Iron Key in Repair Bay
- Mithril Ore ×5 -> Mithril Ingot in Great Forge
- Mithril Ingot + Gear Mould -> Filled Gear Mould in Mould Forge
- Filled Gear Mould -> Mithril Gear in Great Forge

Additionally, on difficulties other than Bearzerker, you can use the machines in
the Mould Forge to make ammo:

- Iron Ingot -> Fragfire Can
- Iron Ingot -> Spikes
- Iron Ingot + Red Crystal ×3 -> Boltmag

On Bearzerk, a different set of machines (and thus checks) is available:

- Iron Ingot -> Axe
- Iron Ingot + Red Crystal ×6 -> Fire Hammer
- Iron Ingot ×8 -> Great Axe

The Iron Ore -> Iron Ingot machine can be used four times, representing the four
ingots (in addition to the four found lying around in the level) needed to craft
the Great Axe in Bearzerk mode.

TODO: using it the Nth time should require you to have found N iron ore.

The upper caves, normally accessible using the Earth Key, can also be reached
using the Axe Key via the maze, which connects the upper caves to the magma
chamber.

The trigger to open the east hall is forging the mithril gear on the anvil. Note
that you don't actually need to get a gear from it; it's the process of forging,
not the item you get, that causes the door to open. However, you *will* need the
gear to actually exit the level; Zan will refuse to arm the explosives if you
don't have it.
